@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture;error-handling] storage-transport-independence
Storage and resource modules MUST return transport-independent errors and MUST NOT import tonic or
construct gRPC statuses. Conversions to API statuses MUST live in the API layer.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] strongly-typed-resource-errors
Resource domain errors MUST use an Error enum defined in the resource module, with distinct variants
for failures callers need to distinguish. They MUST be returned through Result, directly or wrapped
in storage::Error<Error>, and MUST NOT be reduced to strings or anyhow::Error. Callers MUST match
variants instead of parsing error messages. Database and stored-data decoding failures MAY propagate
as FdbBindingError.
